      "text": " <think>\nTo determine which option is a pure public product, we need to understand the definition provided: a pure public product is one where the consumption by one person does not reduce the consumption by another person. This implies that the product must be non-rivalrous and non-excludable.\n\nLet's analyze each option:\n\nA) National defense of a country:\n- National defense is a non-rivalrous good because one person's defense does not diminish another person's defense.\n- National defense is also non-excludable because it is difficult to prevent people from benefiting from it.\n- Therefore, national defense fits the definition of a pure public product.\n\nB) Expressway tolls due to congestion:\n- Expressway tolls are rivalrous because if one person uses the expressway, it reduces the capacity for others to use it.\n- Therefore, expressway tolls do not fit the definition of a pure public product.\n\nC) Free parks built in the city:\n- Free parks are non-rivalrous because one person's use of the park does not reduce another person's use.\n- However, parks are typically excludable because they can be restricted to certain individuals or groups.\n- Therefore, free parks do not fit the definition of a pure public product.\n\nD) Free gifts provided by the mall:\n- Free gifts are rivalrous because if one person receives a gift, it reduces the number of gifts available for others.\n- Therefore, free gifts do not fit the definition of a pure public product.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct option is A.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA\n</answer>",
