ctiveness because participants cannot discuss issues freely, then ensuring freedom of expression is necessary to maintain the effectiveness of the forum. This directly supports the conclusion that we should ensure Internet users have at least as much freedom of expression as did people speaking in the public square.\n\nTherefore, the assumption required by the argument is option D.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
