e is normal, some ultraviolet light reaches the earth's surface.\n- This option directly addresses the concern about the Antarctic ozone layer. If even where the amount of atmospheric ozone is normal, some ultraviolet light reaches the Earth's surface, it implies that the Antarctic ozone layer's decrease could still allow harmful ultraviolet radiation to reach the Earth, potentially damaging polar marine life. This directly undermines the government officials' position that global atmospheric ozone levels remained constant and thus the Antarctic ozone layer's decrease was not a significant concern.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, the one that most seriously undermines the government officials' position is option D.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
