ber of the project team.\n- If Xun Chen is a member, then Yan Zi's statement is satisfied (Xun Chen is invited).\n- This combination is possible.\n\n**Option D: Yan Zi, Meng Shen**\n- If Yan Zi is the host, according to Yan Zi's statement, Zeng Yin or Xun Chen must be a member of the project team.\n- If Meng Shen is a member, then Zeng Yin's statement is satisfied (Meng Shen is invited).\n- This combination is possible.\n\nNow, let's check if any of these combinations violate the constraints:\n- If Yan Zi is the host, Zeng Yin or Xun Chen must be a member.\n- If Zeng Yin is the host, Yan Zi or Meng Shen must be a member.\n- If Xun Chen is the host, Yan Zi must be a member.\n- If Meng Shen is the host, either Xun Chen or Yan Zi must be a member.\n\nGiven these constraints, we need to ensure that no more than two members are included in the project team and no more than one moderator is selected.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, we find that **Option D: Yan Zi, Meng Shen** is the only combination that is impossible because:\n- If Yan Zi is the host, Zeng Yin or Xun Chen must be a member.\n- If Meng Shen is a member, then Zeng Yin's statement is satisfied (Meng Shen is invited).\n- However, if Yan Zi is the host, Zeng Yin or Xun Chen must be a member, and if Meng Shen is a member, then Zeng Yin's statement is satisfied, but this creates a conflict with the requirement that no more than two members are included in the project team.\n\nTherefore, the impossible combination is **Option D: Yan Zi, Meng Shen**.\n\n**Final Answer: D**\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
