anning.\n\nD) Employed people who have three-day breaks from work when holidays are celebrated on Mondays or Fridays:\n- This group is already affected by the current calendar system, as anniversaries do not fall on the same day of the week each year.\n- The proposed change would directly impact their work schedule, as it would ensure that holidays fall on the same day of the week each year. This would mean that holidays like Christmas (December 25) and New Year's Day (January 1) would fall on the same day of the week each year, leading to consistent three-day breaks from work.\n\nGiven this analysis, the group most likely to experience continued scheduling conflicts if the proposed change were implemented is:\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
