ent states that maintaining a political system where candidates adhere to their principles is a vested interest of society. Therefore, if the government financing of campaigns helps to further this vested interest, it would justify the conclusion that the government should finance candidates' campaigns.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, the principle that most justifies the conclusion as it is drawn in the argument is option D.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
