ests that with current shipbuilding technology, large ships can indeed pass through the bridge, which casts doubt on the necessity of demolishing and rebuilding the bridge.\n\nAfter analyzing all the options, option D is the one that most directly challenges the expert's claim by providing a solution that does not require the demolition and rebuilding of the Nanjing Bridge.\n</think>\n<answer>\nD\n</answer>",
